00:19:31,388 --> 00:19:32,989
[SPEAKER_02]: It isn't.

171
00:19:33,009 --> 00:19:42,633
[SPEAKER_02]: The task is to learn how to see that sense of self as elusive, how to see it as an elusive phenomenon.

172
00:19:43,353 --> 00:19:53,357
[SPEAKER_02]: The task is to stop trying to overly define it or see it as a thing that's object of your perception, because it's always in the background.

173
00:19:54,129 --> 00:20:13,856
[SPEAKER_02]: Because for as long as you have those assumptions that you can find it on the level of perceiving it directly, you are disqualifying yourself from actually being able to see it, because it can only be seen on its own terms, and those terms are the terms of an elusive phenomenon, an ambiguous background phenomena, and you have to start seeing it as such.

174
00:20:16,377 --> 00:20:22,799
[SPEAKER_02]: And then you realize you don't need to see it in any more defined manner, because

175
00:20:24,993 --> 00:20:34,404
[SPEAKER_02]: Whether it's an elusive phenomena, whether it's a clear phenomena, whether it's the phenomena in the immediacy or the reflection, the foreground, the background, phenomena is there.

176
00:20:34,665 --> 00:20:36,467
[SPEAKER_02]: It doesn't matter what kind of it is.

177
00:20:37,168 --> 00:20:38,549
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's what you want to be discerning.

178
00:20:39,851 --> 00:20:43,816
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's how you can start including that sense of self, no matter how elusive it is.

